title: peculiar_curiosities
---
<<fade_out YarnCommands 0>><<wait 1>><<picture YarnCommands placeholder>><<fade_in YarnCommands 1>><<bloom_text YarnCommands "Peculiar Curiosities">>
You push open the door to a house that shouldn't still be standing. Inside, apparatus covers every surface and interesting contraptions and tools could be found among everything.
Galvanometer, Beakers, Spectroscope, Gyroscope, Distillation unit, Astrolabe, and a Retort.
Somehow, you can recognize and name each apparatus without hesitation.
But why?
Amid the mess, one particular item stands out.
A "Duplicator".
A note beside it claims that this is one the greatest invention ever made by 'Grandmaster Dwarf Tinkerer Sovenhau'. Apparently, through the use of ritual runes, the device can bring a perfect replica of an object into reality.
What a remarkable invention! A device like this could change a person's life!
-> Use the device #paneldetails=Duplicate_1_card_from_your_deck._Lose_20_Health.
    You carefully place your supplies into the device. The machine whirls into life.
    The crystal lens blazes white-hot and for a moment you feel burns searing through your skin.
    And then...
    <<sfx YarnCommands explode>>
    <<flash YarnCommands red 0.3>>
    <<change_health 20>>
    The blast throws you against the wall. Your ears ringing, sharpnels can be seen piercing into your skin.
    As the dust settles, you see something emerging from the smoke.
    <<duplicate_card YarnCommands>>
    It's your supplies! Its edges curled black, but otherwise a perfect replica.
    You gather the supplies and nurse your injuries. At least now you know the machine works...
    ...Once.
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
-> THIS one's more interesting, though... #paneldetails=Gain_3_Capacity.
    You drop the device and take a gander at the table; Something else catches your eye.
    There lies a simple, sturdy belt. Looks worn-out...
    Magnificent! What a lifesaver! You could use the extra space!
    You took the belt and strap it around your waist before leaving the premises, pleased with your findings.
    <<change_capacity 3>>
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
===
